1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,100
DAD, I CAN'T. IT'S THE SOAP THING.

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:07,300
JADA. WE TALKED ABOUT THIS.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:09,000
TALKED ABOUT WHAT?

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,900
YOU'RE PUTTING ME IN A HOME?

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,200
MAMA. WE WERE GONNA WAIT TILL AFTER CAKE.

6
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,800
ON MY BIRTHDAY?

7
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:22,700
SOAP. YOU THINK I CAN'T RINSE A POT?

8
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:25,600
EVERY DINNER SINCE CHRISTMAS. WE'VE ALL NOTICED.

9
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:27,300
ALL OF YOU?

10
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:30,100
TASTE BUDS GO AS YOU GET OLDER.

11
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:35,000
BUT IF YOU CAN'T TASTE SOAP, WHAT HAPPENS WHEN YOU CAN'T SMELL GAS?

12
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:38,600
I'VE COOKED IN THIS KITCHEN FOR FORTY-TWO YEARS.

13
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:43,000
I KNOW. THAT'S WHY I DON'T WANT YOU IN IT ALONE.

14
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,600
WRENFIELD HAS A UNIT OPENING THIS MONTH. I PUT DOWN A DEPOSIT.

15
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:49,400
YOU ALREADY PAID?

16
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:52,400
NO, SHE WON'T FIGHT IT. SHE'S — SLIPPING.

17
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:57,100
GRANDMA, IT'S STILL THERE.

18
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:01,200
I SCRUBBED THAT PAN THREE TIMES. NEW SOAP. NEW SPONGE.

19
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,700
AND I CAN'T TASTE A THING.

20
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:06,100
JADA, AM I LOSING IT?

21
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:09,500
I LOVE YOU, GRANDMA.

22
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:16,100
WASN'T SHE THE ONE PUSHING YOU INTO WRENFIELD?

23
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:17,400
SHE SURE WAS.

24
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:21,400
NOW SHE'S HERE EVERY SUNDAY, TAKING PLATES HOME. WHAT CHANGED?

25
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:24,700
SHE TOLD ME MY COOKING TASTED LIKE SOAP.

26
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:27,100
MINE TOO.

27
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:28,900
SHOW ME YOUR KITCHEN.

28
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:30,600
WHEN'D YOU BUY THESE?

29
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:34,600
AFTER THANKSGIVING. TERRANCE SENT ME AN ARTICLE ABOUT BLACK PLASTIC.

30
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:37,100
AND WHEN DID THE SOAP START?

31
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:39,400
CHRISTMAS.

32
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,600
SMELL IT.

33
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,400
THAT'S MY DISH SOAP.

34
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,200
IT SOAKS UP WHATEVER SOAP YOU USE.

35
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:48,400
THE MINUTE IT GETS HOT, OUT IT COMES.

36
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:50,500
BUT I CAN'T TASTE IT.

37
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:54,100
NEITHER COULD I. COOK'S ALWAYS THE LAST TO NOTICE.

38
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:58,300
THEY TESTED SILICONE BAKING PANS. IN THE OVEN, CHEMICALS LEACHED OUT.

39
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:01,600
SOME OF THEM ARE LINKED TO HORMONE DISRUPTION.

40
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:06,600
I THREW ALL MINE OUT AND GOT THESE.

41
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:09,800
WOOD? THE CHEAP ONES BLEED IN THE POT.

42
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,200
THAT'S THE FINISH, NOT THE WOOD.

43
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:16,900
EVERY PIECE IS ONE BLOCK OF WOOD. NO GLUE. NOTHING PAINTED ON.

44
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:20,500
THEY'RE CALLED ACAWOOD. I JUST TEXTED YOU THE LINK.

45
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:25,100
KEEP THESE TILL YOURS COME.

46
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:27,500
MOVERS COME SATURDAY AT NINE, MAMA.

47
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:28,800
SMELL THIS FIRST.

48
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:31,400
MAMA. THIS ISN'T ABOUT A SPATULA.

49
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,800
SMELL IT, TERRANCE.

50
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,400
THAT'S DISH SOAP.

51
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:38,700
NOW DOROTHY'S. SHE COOKS WITH IT EVERY DAY.

52
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:39,900
NOTHING.

53
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,400
ONE SNIFF. MY NOSE IS FINE.

54
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,600
YOU'RE THE ONE WHO SENT ME THAT ARTICLE.

55
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:48,200
SMELLING'S ONE THING, MAMA. TASTING'S ANOTHER.

56
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:51,800
FRIDAY NIGHT, I'M MAKING MY POTATO SALAD. EVERYBODY COMES.

57
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:57,500
IF ANYBODY TASTES SOAP, I'LL GET IN YOUR CAR SATURDAY AND NEVER SAY A WORD.

58
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:58,800
DEAL.

59
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:03,700
JADA. YOU FIRST. YOU'RE THE HONEST ONE.

60
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:06,800
GRANDMA.

61
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:08,700
THERE'S NO SOAP. NONE.

62
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:12,300
MAMA. I'M SO SORRY.

63
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:15,700
UNPACK MY BOWLS, TERRANCE.

64
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:16,800
SECONDS?

65
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:23,300
MY SON ALMOST MOVED ME OUT OF MY OWN KITCHEN. OVER THIS.

66
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:27,500
BEFORE ANYBODY TELLS YOU YOU'VE LOST YOUR TOUCH, SMELL YOUR SPATULA.

67
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:31,400
IF IT SMELLS LIKE DISH SOAP, SO DOES YOUR DINNER.

68
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:37,100
AND IF IT'S YOUR WIFE'S COOKING, OR YOUR MAMA'S? SMELL HERS BEFORE YOU BLAME HER.

69
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:42,800
MINE ARE ACAWOOD NOW. SEVEN PIECES, EACH ONE CUT FROM A SINGLE BLOCK OF WOOD.

70
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:48,300
NOTHING ON THEM BUT OIL OR WAX. HERE'S ONE IN HOT WATER. STILL CLEAR.

71
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:49,1000
HAND WASH, DRY, DONE.

72
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:56,500
EIGHTY-NINE NINETY-FIVE WITH THE HOLDER. FREE SHIPPING IN THE U.S., AND NINETY-DAY RETURNS.

73
00:03:56,500 --> 00:04:00,400
THE LINK'S RIGHT BELOW. AND MY KITCHEN? STILL MINE.

